From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: the taskbar as the prototype draws it

The approved Windows 11 prototype (PS5_Proton prototypes/windows11-shell) draws Windows 11's 23H2 taskbar: centred,
Start, the 220 x 32 search pill, Task View and the pinned apps (File Explorer, Settings, Notepad, Terminal), each a 40 x 40
slot 44 px apart; at the right the hidden-icons chevron, the network, volume and battery status button, the two-line
clock and an 8 px show-desktop sliver. Explorer's taskbar showed Start and the open windows only. At 96 DPI it now:

- places every slot where the prototype does (PS5_Proton src/pw_taskbar_layout.h, equal to the prototype's boxes);
- draws the prototype's own pixels in them (pw_shell_taskbar.h: sprites PS5_Proton measured from the prototype and
  premultiplied, GdiAlphaBlend over the cleared glass buffer, so the compositor puts them over the acrylic as Chromium
  put them over the bar), at rest, hovered, pressed and focused, with the 6 x 3 running and 16 x 3 accent pills;
- shows a pinned app's windows on its pin (by process image; Terminal's console window is conhost's) and launches
  the app from it, the other windows after the pins with their own icon on the same plates;
- draws the clock in the prototype's own glyphs where Chromium places them (PS5_Proton src/pw_text_glyphs.h: each
  character measured at Skia's four quarter-pixel pen phases, linear advances, right-aligned by Blink's 1/64 px box;
  GDI's whole-pixel advances made "10/16/2026" 58 px wide instead of 61.1), when every character was measured;
- draws the bar's top line as the prototype's inset divider (black at 5.9%, white at 8.2% in dark), over the
  prototype's taskbar acrylic (the private backdrop of server patch 1141) instead of Mica.

Search opens Start. Task View, the hidden icons and Quick Settings have no native surface yet, so those buttons are
drawn and not wired. At other DPIs the previous drawing stays.
